Only encountered this twice.
  Your pet was in a pit and you pushed a boulder on top of them.  The
boulder did not fill in the pit, it's sitting on the rim.  Just like
you do when you escape a pit or climb out of it.

  You probably can't #untrap your pet because there's no place for it
to go once #untrapped except back into the pit.

  Back away & wait.  Your pet should eventually climb out of the pit
on its own.  Hope it's to your side.

  Once that happens, push the boulder.  Two things will happen
1) the boulder will fill the *next* pit
2) you will be sucked by air currents down into the first pit.


  Only way I know of to fill the pits out of sequence.


